 ],
 "text": "If you tried to throw a package from New York to LA, it would land about 400 feet away, on your own sidewalk. Now, if you built a catapult half a mile long and launched the box at 14,000 miles an hour, it would leave the atmosphere, coast over Kansas, and come down in Los Angeles about 15 minutes later. The box arrives, mostly. And the invoice still comes out right because ContentSystems.ai checked every line."
